WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:11.870
Vibrio cholerae is a pathogenic bacterium that causes a 

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:14.590
terrible disease that's called cholera,

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:16.350
so it's named after the bacterium.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:21.350
It's estimated that there are hundreds of thousands of cases of cholera a 

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:21.950
year.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:27.230
People get cholera from eating or drinking contaminated food or water,

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:29.610
and so cholera can get into the water supply,

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:33.720
and when people ingest cholera and it gets into their bodies,

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:38.320
it causes a disease that causes this massive 

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:40.570
diarrhea that people get,

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:44.960
and they can actually die from cholera, from dehydration during this acute 

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:45.670
phase.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:48.180
And so cholera is prevalent in the world;

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:52.150
it's prevalent in places that don't always have access to clean water.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:57.180
So typically poorer countries or countries that are undergoing civil strife 

00:00:57.180 --> 00:01:00.510
or wars or catastrophes like earthquakes,

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:02.850
where the water supply gets interrupted.

00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:07.710
And it's this very insidious bacterium because its 

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:11.420
strategy is not to stay in the host,

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:12.720
the human host, forever.

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:16.400
So it gets in when people drink contaminated water,

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:18.790
it multiplies like crazy,

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:22.950
it releases all of these toxins that give you the illness,

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:24.600
the symptoms, the diarrhea,

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:29.980
and then it's multiplying in people's gut, and it gets out by 

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:32.720
the gazillions out into the environment,

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:35.710
and then the strategy is then to go infect the next person.

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:38.550
So it's sort of comes in, guns loaded,

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:40.250
it's very infectious,

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:43.880
and it gets out at very high numbers to do it again.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:47.650
When I think about the arc of this field,

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:50.810
it started in this marine bacterium,

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:52.610
it was bioluminescent,

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:57.300
and that's a Vibrio. Those bacterium's names were Vibrio harveryi and 

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:58.350
Vibrio fischeri,

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:03.480
and they are beautiful, glow in the dark, marine Vibrios that 

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:04.890
are not pathogens.

00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:08.720
Cholera is a marine Vibrio,

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:13.470
it's a cousin to the quorum sensing originator Vibrios, its 

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:14.320
pathogenic.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:19.270
So the original bacteria used quorum sensing to unify the 

00:02:19.270 --> 00:02:20.730
production of bioluminescence.

00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:25.870
Cholera uses quorum sensing to unify its pathogenicity,

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:27.930
you know, it's virulence program.

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:33.060
So if you make in the lab Vibrio cholorae mutants that can't talk or they can't 

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:36.980
hear so they don't have quorum sensing, they're not pathogenic in a mouse model.

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:42.380
So that made us think that perhaps if we could deliberately interfere 

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:46.090
with cholerae quorum sensing with small molecules,

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:51.370
maybe those could be medicines. And if they're small molecules, and we could make them 

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:52.000
potent,

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:53.680
and if we could make them specific,

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:55.620
and if we could make them cheaply,

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:56.280
not me,

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:56.980
but somebody,

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:02.820
right, maybe you could help hundreds of thousands or millions of people who 

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:05.980
simply aren't going to have access to clean water.

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:07.210
And that,

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:08.280
to me,

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:13.080
would be a remarkable outcome of the quorum sensing field.

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:15.790
Given that it never started,

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:16.980
the field didn't start,

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:17.980
for that reason.

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:22.250
We didn't even know pathogens used quorum sensing.

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:22.480
Remember,

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:24.790
it started in this glow in the dark bacterium.

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:30.470
And so I think it would be really nice if from that, sort of, anomalous 

00:03:30.470 --> 00:03:32.180
finding from this goofy,

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:33.020
beautiful,

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:37.580
harmless bacteria, ended up teaching us how to 

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:42.370
make a medicine for people that don't have access to medicines routinely,

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:45.280
that would be a great day for this field.

